## 4. P1 — UNIVERSAL ROUTING ENGINE

Implement or complete these relationships using existing schema where possible:

Source → many videos
Video → many generated clips
Clip/video → many destination accounts
Destination account → many scheduled jobs

Required examples:

A. Source A → YouTube Main + YouTube Decider.

B. Video 1 → YouTube Main at 10:00 + Instagram 1 at 18:00.

C. Video 2 → YouTube Decider at 11:00 + Facebook Page 1 at 19:00.

D. Video 3 → YouTube Main + Decider + all selected supported social accounts.

E. Video 4 and Video 5 → same YouTube account, each with its own posting time.

F. Source A and Source B → different destination combinations.

The owner must be able to change these mappings without changing unrelated videos or jobs.

Each destination job must store:
- immutable destination_connection_id
- platform and external account identity
- source/video/clip ID
- schedule and timezone
- metadata profile
- publishing policy
- media variant
- idempotency key
- status, retry count and remote result

Use a parent distribution batch and independent child destination jobs
if that fits the existing architecture.

Prevent duplicate jobs/uploads with database constraints and idempotency.
One failed destination must not stop successful or pending destinations.

Support accurate PARTIAL_SUCCESS, BLOCKED, RETRY and SUCCESS states.

